# 🌐 Networking – Ports

A port is a logical endpoint used to identify a particular service or application on a device.

Example:

```text
192.168.1.20:22
             ↑
            SSH
```

---

# Important Ports

|  Port | Service |
| ----: | ------- |
|    22 | SSH     |
|    53 | DNS     |
| 67/68 | DHCP    |
|    80 | HTTP    |
|   443 | HTTPS   |
|   445 | SMB     |
|  3389 | RDP     |

### Important Corrections

```text
22 → SSH
80 → HTTP
443 → HTTPS
445 → SMB
3389 → RDP
```

These ports should eventually become automatic interview answers.

