# 🎤 Interview Wording Practice

Today's main lesson was improving technical wording.

Instead of:

> "GPO manages groups."

Use:

> **"A GPO is a collection of configuration settings that can be centrally applied to users and computers."**

Instead of:

> "Port is a window where traffic flows."

Use:

> **"A port is a logical endpoint used to identify a specific service or application on a device."**

Instead of:

> "DNS changes the domain into IP."

Use:

> **"DNS translates domain names into IP addresses so devices can locate network services."**

Instead of:

> "Firewall blocks bad things."

Use:

> **"A firewall monitors and controls network traffic based on predefined rules."**

---

# 🧠 Interview Answer Formula

For many technical interview questions, use:

```text
Definition
     ↓
Purpose
     ↓
Example
```

### Example – DNS

**Definition:**

> DNS is a network service that translates domain names into IP addresses.

**Purpose:**

> It allows users to access services using names instead of remembering IP addresses.

**Example:**

> When a user enters a website name, DNS helps resolve that name to the appropriate IP address.

